#===============================================================================
# FILTRE PATH OF EXILE 2 — Ice Shot Deadeye (Early Endgame)
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Objectif    : accumulation de CURRENCY + bases de CRAFT pour la build
# Build       : Arc / Carquois / Evasion (DEX), hybride EV-ES en option
# Severite    : semi-stricte (cache le bruit, garde tout ce qui compte)
# Alertes     : sons + icones minimap + faisceaux actifs
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Installation : copier ce fichier dans
#   Documents/My Games/Path of Exile 2/
# puis l'activer dans Options > Game > Item Filter.
#
# Note : si le jeu signale une ligne en erreur (un nom de Class/BaseType qui
# aurait change avec un patch), envoie-moi la ligne et je la corrige.
#===============================================================================


#===============================================================================
# NOTES DE LA BUILD  (guide @Fubgun — Ice Shot Deadeye S5)
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gear vise :
#   Arc      : Obliterator Bow     Casque  : Desert Cap (-> Subterfuge Mask / Ancestral Tiara)
#   Carquois : Volant Quiver       Torse   : Corsair Coat
#   Bottes   : Cavalry Boots (-> Bladed Shoes)
#   Anneaux  : Prismatic Ring      Amulette: Stellar Amulet      Ceinture: Rawhide Belt
#
# Mandatory Stats: Make sure to fill out your resist, you want 75% fire/cold/lightning
#   resist. Chaos resist is good, but not mandatory to have 75%, I usually aim for 30-50%.
#   You'll also most likely need 1-2 attribute rolls on gear, belt will solve strength and
#   if you need intelligence, get it on a ring or amulet.
# Rings/glove: try to focus on high flat damage to attacks, preferable cold/phys.
# Bow: You want the highest dps ele/phys weapon you can afford. Obliterator Bow is usually
#   the go to, as it has very high base damage and the downside is negligible. Check the
#   notes at the bottom of the guide to learn how to craft a bow.
# Greater Iron Rune will provide the highest dps.
# Quiver: Just good dps stats, high flat/bow dmg or projectile speed with attack speed.
#   Ideally just aim for 3-4 stats from the quiver shown in the gear preview.
# Amulet: Preferable want +proj levels. Crit chance/crit damage is also good, once you swap
#   to crit. Attributes/resist are also fine here. You need at least 30 spirit on the amulet
#   to use all spirit gems.
# Helmet: At the start just look for a high life/evasion/resist helmet, eventually we'll swap
#   to a pure ES helmet with Subterfuge Mask, but you probably wont have a good one for early
#   mapping.
# Chest: you want the highest evasion chest you can afford, this is very important for defense,
#   specially when combined with Beastial Skin on the passive tree. Use Greater Iron Rune.
# Boots: You want the highest movement speed boots you can afford, it's a very important stat.
#   Besides that look for high life/resistance.
# Belt: Not a lot of choices here, just Life/str/resist, eventually you want to get a Headhunter.
# Rarity is still really good in 0.5, try to hit at least 100% if you want to farm efficiently
#   (don't focus on this if you feel like you're lacking damage or defense).
# Jewels on tree: generic damage: attack damage, elemental damage, movement speed, bonus from
#   quivers, projectile damage, attack speed, crit chance, crit damage, etc. Eventually you'll
#   also want Heart of the Well with double "gain as extra" and Against the Darkness with
#   double "gain as extra" as well.
# Important: 1 sapphire jewel with mana on kill to sustain mana during mapping. For bosses,
#   Mark of Siphoning II on Freezing Mark with Eternal Mark should give enough sustain.
# Anoint (Damage): Serrated Edges — cheap and effective once you swap to crit.
#
# Mana Issues:
#   Reminder: always run one jewel with 2% mana on kill.
#   1) Run a regular mana flask with increased recovery + 2% mana on kill jewel.
#   2) Take Conservative Casting for 3 passive points.
#   3) Drop Wind Dancer for Mana Remnants (Harmonic Remnants II, Remnant Potency III,
#      Khatal's Rejuvenation — for Khatal you need Dialla's Desire or 1 point into herald
#      reservation).
#===============================================================================


#===============================================================================
# 1) CURRENCY  (priorite n°1)
#===============================================================================

# --- Tier S : Mirror / Divine / Perfect Jeweller's (ne JAMAIS rater) ----------
Show
    Class "Stackable Currency"
    BaseType "Mirror of Kalandra" "Divine Orb" "Perfect Jeweller's Orb" "Hinekora's Lock"
    SetFontSize 45
    SetTextColor 255 0 0 255
    SetBorderColor 255 0 0 255
    SetBackgroundColor 255 255 255 255
    PlayAlertSound 6 300
    MinimapIcon 0 Red Star
    PlayEffect Red

# --- Tier A : grosses orbes (Exalted / Chaos / Annul / Regal / Vaal / Jeweller) -
Show
    Class "Stackable Currency"
    BaseType "Exalted Orb" "Chaos Orb" "Orb of Annulment" "Regal Orb" "Vaal Orb" "Greater Jeweller's Orb" "Fracturing Orb"
    SetFontSize 44
    SetTextColor 255 255 255 255
    SetBorderColor 255 160 0 255
    SetBackgroundColor 120 40 0 255
    PlayAlertSound 2 300
    MinimapIcon 0 Yellow Diamond
    PlayEffect Yellow

# --- Tier B : currency de craft moyenne ---------------------------------------
Show
    Class "Stackable Currency"
    BaseType "Orb of Alchemy" "Orb of Chance" "Artificer's Orb" "Gemcutter's Prism" "Lesser Jeweller's Orb" "Glassblower's Bauble"
    SetFontSize 40
    SetTextColor 255 255 255 255
    SetBorderColor 255 200 90 255
    SetBackgroundColor 70 40 0 255
    PlayAlertSound 1 250
    MinimapIcon 1 Yellow Circle
    PlayEffect Yellow

# --- Tier C : currency de base (transmute/aug/whetstone...) --------------------
Show
    Class "Stackable Currency"
    BaseType "Orb of Transmutation" "Orb of Augmentation" "Blacksmith's Whetstone" "Arcanist's Etcher" "Armourer's Scrap"
    SetFontSize 35
    SetTextColor 220 220 220 255
    SetBorderColor 120 120 120 255
    MinimapIcon 2 Grey Circle

# --- Filet de securite : TOUTE autre currency reste visible -------------------
Show
    Class "Stackable Currency"
    SetFontSize 38
    SetTextColor 255 255 255 255
    SetBorderColor 200 200 200 255
    MinimapIcon 1 White Circle
    PlayEffect White


#===============================================================================
# 2) MATERIAUX DE CRAFT  (runes, soul cores, omens)
#===============================================================================

# --- Soul Cores (craft / pricey) ----------------------------------------------
